1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,966
[beeping]

2
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:14,931
[humming happily]

3
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:16,349
[Anzu] It's finally here.

4
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:17,934
Ishiai Koji's cat book!

5
00:00:18,017 --> 00:00:20,520
I love that Mom sends
pictures of Momohiki,

6
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:22,772
but this is an extra cat boost for my day.

7
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:25,316
Let the healing begin!
[smooches]

8
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:29,446
[Anzu] Huh? Has it already been a month
since Kazuki moved in?

9
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:32,782
Guess he'll be finding a new place soon.

10
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:36,870
Living with Junta and Kazuki
has been surprisingly fun.

11
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:39,164
It'll be strange when he moves out.

12
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:40,749
ARISA: CAN WE MEET?

13
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:43,293
[Anzu] Speaking of strange, I wonder
who that text was from--

14
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:44,836
-[man] I know, right?
-[grunts]

15
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:45,962
-[can clanks]
-[man grunts]

16
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:47,088
[Anzu] My book!

17
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:49,215
[sighs in relief]

18
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,093
What the hell do you think you're doing?

19
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:54,679
I was just waiting
for the light to change.

20
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:58,099
[Anzu] He bumped into me.
I should be the one yelling.

21
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:00,977
It's all thanks to you
that I dropped my coffee.

22
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,812
-And ruined my shoes.
-[gasps]

23
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,814
-[man] You're gonna pay for that!
-[Anzu] Hey!

24
00:01:05,648 --> 00:01:06,941
-Uh…
-That's enough.

25
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:09,069
[Anzu] Huh?

26
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:12,072
You're the one who bumped into her.

27
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:14,282
[gasping]

28
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:17,285
Ah, dude. You're, like, crazy hot.

29
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:20,789
What do you say, you pay back
your little friend's debt with a date?

30
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:22,207
[man laughing mischievously]

31
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:25,376
[grunts in pain]

32
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,629
-Don't ever touch me.
-[man] Ow…

33
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:29,297
Now apologize to her.

34
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:31,800
It's just a stupid book!

35
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:33,760
[grunts]
Just a book?

36
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:37,514
[Anzu] You have no idea what I've lost!

37
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:39,808
[shouting] This book is worth
hours of healing!

38
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:43,978
I curse you!
May stray cats infest your house

39
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,897
and soak your bed in cat pee!

40
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:48,149
You're gonna drill straight into my brain!

41
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,901
-[growling]
-[screams]

42
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:51,528
I'm sorry!

43
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:53,905
-[man] Ow!
-Uh…

44
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:57,200
[man] My head… the pain.
That chick's crazy.

45
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:58,368
-[snorts]
-[startled gasps]

46
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:02,914
Maybe next time
you'll be a little bit more respectful.

47
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:05,875
[all gasp]

48
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,503
-Let's go.
-[Anzu blows raspberry]

49
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:11,131
-Your book okay? Sorry about those jerks.
-[gasps]

50
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:12,966
Heh?
[sighs in relief]

51
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:14,801
[Anzu exclaims]

52
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:19,222
Oh yeah, the book's fine.
Thanks for saving me.

53
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:21,015
Oh my gosh, she'll think I'm in love!

54
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:23,977
I hope I don't look as dumb
as I feel right now!

55
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:26,437
Did you really

56
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:28,731
curse him with a cat-pee-soaked mattress?

57
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:31,985
[Anzu] It was all I could think of.
You can never get that smell out.

58
00:02:32,068 --> 00:02:33,194
-[Tsukasa] Arisa.
-[both] Huh?

59
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:35,071
Hey, Tsukasa.

60
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,322
Kazuki?

61
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:38,491
Hoshino? You know each other?

62
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:39,784
Hoshino, like…

63
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:42,620
Wait, are you Anzu Hoshino?

64
00:02:42,704 --> 00:02:43,788
Me? Um…

65
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:46,791
I'm Arisa, Tsukasa's big sister.

66
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:48,501
Thanks for looking after him.

67
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:49,794
[chuckles]

68
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:54,007
Uh, legendary good looks
run in your family.

69
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:56,551
So bright, can't look directly at it!

70
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:57,635
[Tsukasa] You're an idiot.

71
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:04,851
[theme music]

72
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:29,018
[birds chirping]

73
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:31,145
#8 THE PHOENIX RISES! I AM A BIRD!

74
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:35,066
Thanks for having me. Are you sure
that I'm not barging in here?

75
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,234
Of course not.

76
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:39,279
Thanks again
for letting Tsukasa stay here.

77
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:41,197
A month is a long time.

78
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:42,865
No, not at all.

79
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:45,785
Really, it's been awesome
having him around.

80
00:04:45,868 --> 00:04:48,538
[Anzu] Not to mention
this whole thing is my fault.

81
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:52,875
My mother and I
should have introduced ourselves sooner.

82
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:55,336
-To be honest, we were a bit surprised.
-[grumbles]

83
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,463
We didn't think he'd be staying this long.

84
00:04:57,547 --> 00:05:00,925
Between the pipe bursting
and the new phone, it's been chaotic.

85
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:03,261
So I figured it was probably
best for me to come out

86
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:04,929
and get the details in person.

87
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:07,640
Oh yeah, that makes sense.

88
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:11,561
[Anzu] The phone…
Yeah, that was my fault too.

89
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:15,148
Oh. Hey, would you like
something to drink?

90
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:18,192
I think we have some iced tea, or, um…

91
00:05:18,276 --> 00:05:20,778
-[Tsukasa] Uh, there's a fresh pitcher.
-Oh, that would be great.

92
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:21,821
[chuckles]

93
00:05:22,905 --> 00:05:25,908
[Arisa clears throat]
Better let Mom know everything's okay.

94
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:30,330
[Tsukasa] So, did something happen
at the station? You looked frazzled.

95
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:35,293
Oh. This guy bumped into me,
then tried to pick a fight with me.

96
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:36,210
[Tsukasa] What?

97
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:39,922
But your sister totally saved me.

98
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:42,633
Those guys didn't stand a chance.

99
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:44,886
You know what? Your sister's really cool.

100
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:47,055
Yeah, but she had a tendency
to find trouble.

101
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:49,515
I'm sorry that happened.

102
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,142
Nah, it's fine,

103
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:54,937
'cause I cursed him with a mattress
completely soaked in cat pee!

104
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:58,566
-So yeah, it's all good.
-[muffled laugh]

105
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:02,987
[Tsukasa] Seriously?
A mattress soaked in cat pee?

106
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,198
No, it really is the worst!

107
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:06,991
[chuckles]

108
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:10,703
[Anzu] Sorry to keep you waiting.

109
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:12,538
All good, thanks.

110
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:17,085
Kazuki, I'm just curious.

111
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:19,295
Why did you wanna go to our school
and live alone?

112
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:20,797
[both gasp]

113
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,714
[both sigh]

114
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:24,509
[Anzu] Uh, you don't have to answer that.
I shouldn't have asked.

115
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:27,970
-[whimpers]
-Hmm… Well, how do I say this?

116
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,976
-Huh?
-[soft chuckle]

117
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,687
Our father's a real piece of garbage.

118
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:37,605
SHIT

119
00:06:37,688 --> 00:06:39,482
Piece of garbage?

120
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:42,151
Yup. That's why our mom decided

121
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:44,320
it was best for Tsukasa
to go to school out here.

122
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:45,238
Oh.

123
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,407
I'm not wrong, am I?

124
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:49,492
No.

125
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:54,747
I was really worried
when I heard you'd be living alone.

126
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:58,668
I'm relieved you're staying
with someone sweet like Anzu.

127
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,670
[phone vibrates]

128
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:03,256
Oh, Makoto.

129
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:06,384
Um, hey.

130
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,385
What's up?

131
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:12,598
-[Arisa] Who's Makoto?
-[Anzu] He's a friend from school.

132
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:14,267
Oh.

133
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:17,270
Hey, what's Tsukasa like
at school, anyway?

134
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:21,649
Well, uh, he's popular
but keeps to himself.

135
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:25,570
Being reserved makes everyone
like him even more.

136
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:26,821
And you?

137
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:29,740
-You seem to like him too, huh?
-[chokes]

138
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:31,075
[spits, gags]

139
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:32,493
Huh?

140
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:33,494
[in deep voice]
It's not like that.

141
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:35,663
I swear on my unborn descendants.

142
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:36,873
[Arisa] That's a bit extreme.

143
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:40,585
In fact, I didn't like him
when I first met him.

144
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:43,087
But…

145
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:45,381
I'm glad I took the time
to get to know him better.

146
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:48,676
'Cause, you know,
now he's a really great friend.

147
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,179
[Arisa chuckles softly]

148
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:55,224
You know, he used to be
a really social kid.

149
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:58,186
He was always smiling,
befriending everyone he met.

150
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,688
I can't picture that.

151
00:08:00,771 --> 00:08:02,273
[Arisa chuckles]
I know, right?

152
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:06,569
There was a problem
back when he was in junior high.

153
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:09,322
Ever since then, he sort of shut down.

154
00:08:09,405 --> 00:08:13,493
So before, the way he was laughing
with you, I haven't seen that side

155
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:16,329
of my little brother
in a really long time.

156
00:08:16,996 --> 00:08:17,872
Huh?

157
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:20,500
You bring it out of him, Anzu.

158
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,627
Really, it's not--

159
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:23,836
-[door shuts]
-[both] Huh?

160
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,838
He wanted me to go to a movie,

161
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,841
but I think he really just wanted
someone to vent to.

162
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:31,636
-[Anzu] About what?
-Oh…

163
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:34,388
Something about his sister
stealing his last pudding.

164
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:35,348
MAKOTO
IT WAS DELICIOUS

165
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:37,475
[chuckles]
Tell him next time

166
00:08:37,558 --> 00:08:39,018
to write his name on it.

167
00:08:39,101 --> 00:08:40,603
[Tsukasa] He did. She ate it anyway.

168
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:45,149
Hmm. There's no stronger grudge
than one held over food.

169
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:46,484
Is it that big a deal?

170
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,694
I don't make the rules.

171
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:51,572
[light music]

172
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:58,079
About your friend, Anzu.

173
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,374
She's sweet. I'm just surprised
you're friends with her.

174
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:02,291
[chuckles]

175
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:05,002
I thought
you were still avoiding all girls.

176
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:08,714
[sighs]

177
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,592
Yeah, I know. I wasn't planning on it.

178
00:09:12,593 --> 00:09:15,763
But she's different.
I feel more at ease with her.

179
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:19,350
Tsukasa, why don't you just
stay here a while?

180
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:21,060
Huh?

181
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:22,562
Calm down, it's a joke.

182
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:25,022
-[sighs in relief]
-Uh… uh…

183
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,775
Uh, well…

184
00:09:28,317 --> 00:09:30,736
[Anzu] I don't mind if you don't mind.

185
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:31,946
Hm?

186
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:35,116
You've been so helpful around here.

187
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:37,868
And maybe it's just me,
but I think it's been a lot of fun

188
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:38,995
living with you and Junta.

189
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:42,999
[Anzu] Not to mention Riri's scheming
if you leave Junta and I alone.

190
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:44,292
Most importantly,

191
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:47,670
you're the only one brave enough
to kill all those bugs!

192
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:49,005
-[groans]
-[Tsukasa chuckles]

193
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:51,048
If it's that important to you,

194
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:53,301
then I guess I'll stay.

195
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:56,596
Hm.

196
00:09:57,346 --> 00:10:00,516
[sighs in relief]
Yeah? This will be great!

197
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,351
There's another show
I've been dying to watch.

198
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:03,269
Sure.

199
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:07,481
I get it now. That's why
you never wanted to talk about her.

200
00:10:08,858 --> 00:10:11,235
You were embarrassed I'd figure it out.

201
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:12,778
That she makes you smile again.

202
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,156
Um…

203
00:10:17,074 --> 00:10:19,160
-Wait, do you like--
-It's not like that.

204
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:22,246
With Hoshino, I can be myself.

205
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:25,082
For me, that's all I need.

206
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,418
[Tsukasa sighs]

207
00:10:30,004 --> 00:10:31,005
[Arisa] Okay.

208
00:10:31,964 --> 00:10:33,966
[soft music]

209
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:36,385
[water running]

210
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:39,555
[Anzu] I'm glad
I met Kazuki's sister today.

211
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,932
I learned a lot more about him.

212
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:43,893
[door opens]

213
00:10:43,976 --> 00:10:45,311
Hey, you're back.

214
00:10:46,854 --> 00:10:49,106
You have the coolest sister.

215
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,651
I loved getting to meet her.
[gasps]

216
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:54,362
I should have worn something nicer.
This outfit sucks.

217
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:58,908
I really assumed you thought
that outfit was appropriate

218
00:10:58,991 --> 00:10:59,909
to meet guests.

219
00:10:59,992 --> 00:11:01,243
No way.

220
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:03,663
I learned a lot
when we went shopping together.

221
00:11:03,746 --> 00:11:06,415
I've tried to be more mindful
about what I wear since then.

222
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:10,378
[Anzu] Man, I wish I had
a big sister like her.

223
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:12,963
Hoshino.

224
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:15,758
What Arisa said
about why I lived by myself…

225
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:18,761
Yeah?

226
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:20,471
Uh, uh--

227
00:11:21,305 --> 00:11:22,264
[exhales deeply]

228
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:25,476
Never mind. Maybe another day.

229
00:11:27,186 --> 00:11:28,354
Hmm…

230
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,190
[Anzu] Uh, okay.

231
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:36,445
[Anzu] Is it just me or…

232
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,532
-[Riri] Is this warm feeling friendship?
-[grunts]

233
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:42,618
Or is this excitement? Love!

234
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:46,372
Yay! Great job, Anzu, I'm so proud of you!

235
00:11:46,455 --> 00:11:48,749
You were able to get
his big sister's approval,

236
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,418
even just like that.

237
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:52,753
I tell you how can you find love,
it's so fulfilling.

238
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:57,633
-Now, let's keep this up--
-You know what? I didn't miss you one bit!

239
00:11:57,716 --> 00:11:59,343
[Anzu roars]

240
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:02,138
-[slaps]
-Come on!

241
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:03,722
A FEW DAYS LATER

242
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:07,393
In order to address low birth rate issues,

243
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:13,399
Anzu was gifted a real-life dating sim
called Romantic Thriller.

244
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:15,901
And after many perfect scenarios,

245
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:20,573
I am reporting that there has been
zero romantic development.

246
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:22,908
I can't turn this in!

247
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,994
[frustrated groan]

248
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:29,415
Clearly, I have a lot more research to do.

249
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,876
I have an excellent idea!

250
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:33,919
-We can go on a date.
-What?

251
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:37,590
[Riri] I need to experience
what a real-life date is like,

252
00:12:37,673 --> 00:12:39,425
so you and I will go on a mock date.

253
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:40,926
A mock date?

254
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:43,262
What are you even talking about?

255
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:46,015
I'm so over your nonsense.

256
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:49,894
[chuckling]
Aw, don't be such a meanie!

257
00:12:49,977 --> 00:12:50,936
-Ha!
-[explosion]

258
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:54,440
-[Anzu] Huh?
-What if I look like this instead?

259
00:12:54,523 --> 00:12:55,357
[chuckles]

260
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,443
[Anzu] Wait!
There's a boy version of you too?

261
00:12:58,027 --> 00:12:58,986
[groans]

262
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:01,697
Whatever. Doesn't change anything.

263
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:04,200
I'm not asking you to do this for free.

264
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:06,202
-[Anzu] Huh?
-[Rio] I'll buy you those cat pajamas

265
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:08,787
you saw in the mall.
The one with the hoodies and tail.

266
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:11,248
[in deep voice]
It's a deal.

267
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:12,791
[groans in pain]
Let go!

268
00:13:13,542 --> 00:13:16,879
Whoo! Can't believe I'm on my first date!

269
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:18,172
Tell me…

270
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:20,257
[bright music]

271
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:22,676
Why did I have to dress up for this?

272
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,303
It's a date.

273
00:13:24,386 --> 00:13:26,555
We're not hanging out
at a rest stop for truckers.

274
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,891
Hey! Do I really dress that badly?

275
00:13:28,974 --> 00:13:30,434
Yep, just the worst.

276
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:32,937
Now, on with our date!

277
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:33,938
Ugh!

278
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:37,608
-[whimpers]
-Easy there, I'm not some sort of pervert.

279
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:40,444
Holding hands is what you do on dates.

280
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:43,280
I don't care. I don't want people
getting the wrong idea about us.

281
00:13:43,781 --> 00:13:45,950
-[grunts]
-Hmm…

282
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:48,494
[Rio] I'll buy you another cat shirt!

283
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,080
[Anzu grunts]

284
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,457
-Fine, then hold my hand.
-Ow, ow, ouch!

285
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,543
So, where are we going?

286
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:59,630
The most classic of dating activities.
The movies.

287
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:01,298
[laughter]

288
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:05,678
[Rio] A romantic movie always
gets the couple in the mood for love.

289
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,680
Slowly their hands touch.

290
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:09,265
-[girl gasps]
-Huh?

291
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:12,685
[Rio] And then, their lips touch.

292
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:14,395
[smooching]

293
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:15,479
You're twisted.

294
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:18,190
[indistinct chatter]

295
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:22,861
Is there anything good out right now?

296
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:25,531
Oh, any cat movies?

297
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,074
[Rio] No cats! We're on a date,

298
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:28,534
so we're definitely watching
a romantic movie!

299
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:29,869
ETERNAL STAR

300
00:14:30,452 --> 00:14:33,247
What? That looks so lame.

301
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:36,208
One of those tearjerkers
where the girl dies in the end.

302
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:37,626
Tearjerkers are great!

303
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:40,963
So much romance,
it'll be the perfect reference material!

304
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:43,883
Using this kind of movie
is a reference…

305
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:46,051
doesn't bode well for me.

306
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:48,888
[Makoto groans]

307
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:50,764
That was so good!

308
00:14:51,348 --> 00:14:52,892
We've got to do this more often.

309
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:54,894
-[Tsukasa] Yeah.
-[Makoto] Hey, look!

310
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:56,729
-Need the bathroom first.
-[Makoto] Hosshi!

311
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:58,230
-[both] Huh?
-[Makoto] Hey, you!

312
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:00,399
-[Anzu gasps]
-Looking good all dressed up.

313
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:02,651
Kazuki, Makoto.

314
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:04,737
-Huh?
-Uh?

315
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:05,905
[gasps]

316
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:07,907
-[Anzu] Oh crap!
-[Anzu grunting]

317
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:09,283
How's it going?

318
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:12,328
I'm Anzu's cousin, Rio. Rio Fushigi.

319
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:13,871
I'm Riri's twin brother.

320
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:15,664
[Anzu] Yeah, nice backstory.

321
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:17,833
This is just great.
All the people in this town

322
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:19,668
and we had to run into these two?

323
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:21,503
Wait, didn't he set this up?

324
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:24,256
All right, we better get going then.
We're on a date.

325
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,175
-[smacks]
-Hey, don't say stuff like that.

326
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:29,094
Ignore him.
Rio just likes to mess around sometimes.

327
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:30,012
Bye!

328
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:33,432
-See ya, Hosshi. Oh, and Hosshi's cousin.
-[growls]

329
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:36,936
They seem oddly close
for being cousins, don't you think?

330
00:15:37,978 --> 00:15:38,812
[Anzu grunts]

331
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:42,149
What's your problem?

332
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,984
Calm down, it's a mock date.

333
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,653
Gotta treat it like the real thing.

334
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:47,863
You're gonna give them
the wrong idea about me.

335
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:50,032
I'll sue you for defamation!

336
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:52,409
The lady doth protest too much.

337
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:56,580
[Anzu] Strange. Usually, he'd get Kazuki
and the others involved

338
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:58,916
in some crazy dating scenarios.

339
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:02,086
Maybe he really is trying
to learn about dating.

340
00:16:02,169 --> 00:16:03,170
Too bad for him,

341
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:06,423
whatever he learns here,
I'll just destroy it!

342
00:16:07,716 --> 00:16:09,385
-[chuckles mischievously]
-What's with that face?

343
00:16:09,468 --> 00:16:12,429
Smiling weird like that makes you look
like you're coming unhinged.

344
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:15,432
There's nothing better than popcorn
